            "id": "14001072",
            "headline": "Hillhouse-backed managed workspace provider Table Space files IPO papers to raise Rs 800 crore via fresh issue",
            "heading": "Hillhouse-backed managed workspace provider Table Space files IPO papers to raise Rs 800 crore via fresh issue",
            "intro": "Table Space IPO | Promoter AGS TS II Holdings Pte, owned by Hillhouse Investment, will be the largest seller among the selling shareholders, offloading up to 4.98 crore shares through the OFS.",
            "body": "Bengaluru-based managed workspace provider Tablespace Technologies, backed by Singapore-based global alternative investment manager Hillhouse Investment, has filed a draft red herring prospectus (DRHP) with the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) to raise Rs 800 crore through a fresh issue, along with an offer-for-sale (OFS) of 6.54 crore equity shares.\r\n\r\nPromoter AGS TS II Holdings Pte, owned by Hillhouse Investment, will be the largest seller among the selling shareholders, offloading up to 4.98 crore shares through the OFS. Individual promoters Karan Chopra and Kunal Mehra, along with Srinivas Prasad, Narendra Kumar Kamaraju, RSP Real Estate LLP and Ramachandra Venkatasubba Rao, will be the other selling shareholders in the OFS.\r\n\r\nTablespace Technologies may also consider raising up to Rs 160 crore through a pre-IPO round, i.e. before filing the red herring prospectus with the Registrar of Companies. This amount will be part of the fresh issue component. Therefore, if the company raises funds through a pre-IPO placement, the amount raised will be reduced from the fresh issue size.\r\n\r\nCurrently, Hillhouse Investment holds a 41.76 percent stake in the company, followed by Amit Mono Banerji with a 22.14 percent stake and Karan Chopra with a 12.47 percent stake.\r\n\r\nTable Space specialises in providing premium managed workspace solutions through a portfolio comprising 11.46 million square feet of leasable area across 33 key office clusters in eight Tier-1 cities in India: Bengaluru, Mumbai Metropolitan Region (MMR), Hyderabad, Gurugram, Chennai, Pune, Noida and New Delhi.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nThe company proposes to utilise Rs 550 crore of the fresh issue proceeds to repay debt, against total outstanding borrowings of Rs 970.6 crore as of June 2026. The remaining proceeds will be utilised for inorganic growth through unidentified acquisitions and general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nTable Space, which competes with listed peers such as Smartworks Coworking Spaces, Indiqube Spaces, Awfis Space Solutions and WeWork India Management, reported a loss of Rs 403.3 crore for the year ended March 2026, narrowing significantly from a loss of Rs 1,554.1 crore in the previous year.\r\n\r\nRevenue during the same period increased sharply by 66.3 percent to Rs 2,262.3 crore from Rs 1,360.5 crore.\r\n\r\nAxis Capital, BofA Securities India, CLSA India, IIFL Capital Services and JM Financial have been appointed as the merchant bankers for the Tablespace Technologies IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/hillhouse-backed-managed-workspace-provider-table-space-files-ipo-papers-to-raise-rs-800-crore-via-fresh-issue-14001072.html",
