          "1": {
            "id": "14000783",
            "headline": "Business News Live: Escorts Kubota to hike tractor prices across brands in August",
            "heading": "Business News Live: Escorts Kubota to hike tractor prices across brands in August",
            "intro": "Unitree\u2019s Shanghai IPO 5,526 times subscribed by retail buyers",
            "body": "Welcome to Moneycontrol Business Blog. First up, the government has extended the benefits of the e-2W subsidy under the amended PM E-Drive scheme till March 31, 2028. The overall scheme outlay remains capped at Rs 11,900 crore, while individual components will close early once their respective targets are achieved.\r\n\r\nThe subsidy for electric two-wheelers has been reduced to Rs 2,500 per kWh, capped at Rs 5,000, for FY26-FY28. The maximum ex-factory price eligible for the incentive has also been limited to electric two-wheelers priced up to Rs 1.5 lakh. The revised allocation for the e-2W component stands at Rs 2,767 crore, which is expected to support up to 45.79 lakh vehicles.\r\n\r\nThe commercial electric three-wheeler (L5) component has been confirmed as closed since December 26, 2025. Claims under all scheme components must be submitted by December 31, 2027, with no payouts to be made after March 31, 2028.\r\n\r\nNext, Zen Technologies has bagged a supply order worth Rs 295 crore from the Ministry of Defence.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, PC Jeweller reported a strong performance in the first quarter. Consolidated profit rose 37.2% year-on-year to Rs 222.2 crore from Rs 161.9 crore, while revenue increased 21% to Rs 877 crore from Rs 724.9 crore. EBITDA jumped 89.7% to Rs 241.6 crore compared with Rs 127.3 crore in the year-ago period. EBITDA margin expanded to 27.5% from 17.6% a year earlier.\r\n\r\nIn another development, sources indicate that Apar Industries has launched a qualified institutional placement (QIP) to raise funds. The company plans to raise Rs 2,500 crore through the issue, with the indicative price set at Rs 14,805 per share, representing a 9.99% discount to the current market price. The lock-up period for both the company and the promoter has been set at 45 days.",
            "posturl": "news/business/business-news-live-today-on-august-11-corporate-news-q1-results-agm-ipo-latest-updates-subscription-status-liveblog-14000783.html",
