          "2": {
            "id": "14000594",
            "headline": "Milky Mist raises over Rs 465 crore via anchor book ahead of Rs 1,553-crore IPO; Temasek buys more shares",
            "heading": "Milky Mist raises over Rs 465 crore via anchor book ahead of Rs 1,553-crore IPO; Temasek buys more shares",
            "intro": "Milky Mist IPO | Singaporean investment firm Temasek Holdings emerged as the largest buyer in the company through the anchor book.",
            "body": "Chennai-based dairy products maker Milky Mist Dairy Food has raised Rs 465.3 crore from 19 anchor investors on August 10, a day before the IPO opens for public subscription.\r\n\r\nThe company tapped the capital markets to raise up to Rs 1,553 crore through an initial public offering (IPO) at the upper end of the price band of Rs 133-140 per share. The IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 1,428 crore, while promoter Sathishkumar T and his wife, Anitha S, will sell shares worth Rs 125 crore through an offer-for-sale (OFS).\r\n\r\nThe issue will open for public subscription on August 11 and close on August 13, 2026.\r\n\r\nMilky Mist Dairy Food on Monday finalised the allocation of 3.32 crore equity shares through the anchor book at the upper end of the price band.\r\n\r\nSingaporean investment firm Temasek Holdings emerged as the largest buyer in the company through the anchor book. Its subsidiary Zulia Investments Pte picked up 1.14 crore equity shares worth Rs 160 crore (equivalent to 1.48 percent of post issue paid-up equity), while International Finance Corporation bought 14.28 lakh shares for Rs 20 crore.\r\n\r\nTemasek, through Jongsong Investments Pte, already held a 5.16 percent stake in Milky Mist, which was acquired in the pre-IPO round.\r\n\r\nOut of the total allocation of 3.32 crore equity shares to anchor investors, the company allocated 1.53 crore shares to nine domestic mutual funds, including Nippon Life India, HDFC AMC, ICICI Prudential AMC, Invesco MF, Motilal Oswal AMC, Edelweiss, HSBC Mutual Fund, Union MF and Trust AMC, which applied through their 13 schemes, Milky Mist said in its filing with the exchanges.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nAmong others, IIFL Asset Management, India Acorn Fund and Anicut Equity Continuum Fund also invested in the company through the anchor book. Aditya Birla Sun Life Insurance was allocated 7.14 lakh shares worth Rs 10 crore by the company.\r\n\r\nMilky Mist, which makes cheese, paneer, butter, curd, ghee, yogurt, ice cream and ultra-high-temperature long-shelf-life products, will utilise Rs 496.8 crore of the net proceeds from the fresh issue to repay debt, while Rs 469.2 crore will be spent on the expansion and modernisation of its Perundurai manufacturing facility.\r\n\r\nFurther, the company will use Rs 155.3 crore for the deployment of visi coolers, ice cream freezers and chocolate coolers, with the remainder being utilised for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nAs of May 2026, Milky Mist had consolidated outstanding borrowings of Rs 1,390.7 crore.\r\n\r\nThe company offers all its products under the umbrella brand Milky Mist, as well as multiple sub-brands such as SmartChef, Capella and Misty Lite. It operates from a single manufacturing facility in Perundurai, Tamil Nadu.\r\n\r\nJM Financial, Axis Capital and IIFL Capital Services are acting as the merchant bankers for the Milky Mist IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/milky-mist-raises-over-rs-465-crore-via-anchor-book-ahead-of-rs-1-553-crore-ipo-opening-temasek-buys-more-shares-14000594.html",
            "ai_impact_text_option_s": "Bullet",
            "ai_impact_text_s": "* Milky Mist Dairy Food raises Rs 465.3 crore from 19 anchor investors\r\n* Rs 1,553 crore IPO to open on August 11\r\n* Temasek Holdings buys additional 1.14 crore equity shares worth Rs 160 crore",
